  "issue": 370,
  "request": "Goal: Implement Issue 370 by moving flow lifecycle decision ownership from registry.js to definition-side APIs while keeping registry.js as a command registry. Scope: registry.js keeps command metadata and calls a shared lifecycle entry point; definition-side code provides APIs for node lookup, maxAttempts, sideEffects, runtime step resolution, lifecycle resolution, and task node lookup; lifecycle actions are represented by dedicated classes instead of object literal action records; complex finalize/git/filesystem/report behavior remains in normal handler functions reached through a lifecycle hook action; FLOW_DEFINITION and TASK_DEFINITION are no longer exposed as raw exports; steps-array utilities are moved to a separate step-tree module. Out of Scope: removing registry.js, adding dependencies, TypeScript migration, compatibility aliases for old raw exports, or rewriting complex finalize execution as declarative config. Verification: update or add unit tests so registry lifecycle hooks delegate through definition-side APIs, raw definition exports are not imported by callers, step-tree utilities are imported from the new module, and existing review/gate/finalize transitions still produce the expected step statuses and skips.",
